            <ArticleTitle>Osteochondroma of the cervical spine causing occipital nerve neuralgia. Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>777-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Osteochondroma is a rare tumor of the cervical spine. The authors present a rare case of osteochondroma narrowing the C 1/2 foramen and causing occipital neuralgia. Complete removal of the tumor was performed with release of the pain. The literature is reviewed and etiology, diagnosis, treatment and differential diagnosis are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
